    ex:city "Buffalo" ;
    ex:city "Los Angeles" ;
    ex:city "San Diego" ;
    ex:history """The Buffalo Braves were an American professional basketball franchise based in Buffalo, New York. The Braves competed in the National Basketball Association (NBA) as a member club of the league's Eastern Conference Atlantic Division from 1970 until 1978. In 1978, Braves owner John Y. Brown Jr. swapped franchises with then-Boston Celtics owner Irv Levin, who then moved the team to San Diego, where it was renamed the San Diego Clippers. The franchise moved to Los Angeles in 1984, and is now known as the Los Angeles Clippers.""" ;
    ex:logo <https://cdn.nba.com/logos/nba/1610612746/global/L/logo.svg> ;
