ex:team_1610612765
    
    ex:actualName "Detroit Pistons" ;
    ex:teamName "Fort Wayne Pistons" ;
    ex:acronym "DET" ;
    ex:acronym "FTW" ;
    ex:city "Fort Wayne" ;
    ex:city "Detroit" ;
    ex:history """The Detroit Pistons are an American professional basketball team based in Detroit. The Pistons compete in the National Basketball Association (NBA) as a member of the Central Division of the Eastern Conference. The team plays its home games at Little Caesars Arena, located in Midtown Detroit. Founded in Fort Wayne, Indiana as a semi-professional company basketball team called the Fort Wayne Zollner Pistons in 1937, they would turn pro in 1941 as a member of the National Basketball League (NBL), where they won two NBL championships: in 1944 and 1945. The Pistons later joined the Basketball Association of America (BAA) in 1948. The NBL and BAA merged to become the NBA in 1949, and the Pistons became part of the merged league.[1][8] In 1957, the franchise moved to Detroit. The Pistons have won three NBA championships: in 1989, 1990 and 2004.""" ;
    ex:logo <https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c9/Logo_of_the_Detroit_Pistons.svg> ;
    ex:conference ex:conference_1 ;
